# MCP External Server Configuration
#
# Copy this file to mcp-servers.yml and enable the servers you want to use.
# API keys must ONLY be set via environment variables (inline keys are ignored):
#   MCP_{SERVER_ID_UPPER}_API_KEY  (e.g. MCP_NOTION_API_KEY)
#
# Supported transports:
#   - streamable-http (default, recommended)
#   - sse (legacy, used as automatic fallback)
#
# Each server exposes tools that Qalem agents can call during PBL sessions
# and classroom generation. Tools are auto-discovered via MCP protocol.
# Each server MUST have an explicit organizationIds UUID allowlist before activation.
# An absent or empty allowlist denies access to every tenant.
# Docker: mount /app/mcp-servers.yml read-only on both web and worker.
# Alternatively use MCP_SERVERS JSON when no YAML file is present.
# Restart each process after changes; GET /api/admin/mcp probes web connections
# and is restricted to authenticated super-administrators.

# NotebookLM, Notion and Google Drive use the Diwan document API. Direct MCP
# servers for them are deliberately not configured here. See:
# - docs/guides/notebooklm-via-diwan.md
# - docs/guides/notion-via-diwan.md
# - docs/guides/google-drive-via-diwan.md
servers: []
